and

Plain Text
POST /login HTTP/1.1" 404 Not Found
What does 404 mean?

404 Not Found means:

✅ FastAPI server is running
 ❌ Route /login does not exist

Check available routes

Open:

Shell
http://localhost:8000/docs

or run:

Shell
curl http://localhost:8000/openapi.json

You will see all API endpoints.

Check if /login exists

Search in your code:

Shell
grep -rn "@app.post" backend/

or

Shell
grep -rn "login" backend/main.py
 

You should find something like:

Python
@app.post("/login")

If you do not see this line, then the /login API has not been created.

Example Login API
Python
from fastapi import FastAPI
 
app = FastAPI()
 
@app.post("/login")
def login(data: dict):
return {
"message": "login success",
"username": data["username"]
}

Then:

Shell
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/login \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"username":"admin","password":"admin123"}'

returns:

JSON
{
"message":"login success",
"username":"admin"
}
Most likely in your project

Currently you already tested:

Shell
curl http://localhost:8000/predict/hi

and

Shell
curl http://localhost:8000/predict/fakeloginpage

Those worked, which means your app probably only has:

Python
@app.get("/predict/{text}")

and does not have:

Python
@app.post("/login")

That's why FastAPI returns:

JSON
{"detail":"Not Found"}

Run this and show the output:

Shell
grep -n "@app" backend/main.py

It will list all available endpoints in your FastAPI application.
